rblat LICENSE
=============

rblat bundles and directly links the BLAT source code (v35) written by Jim Kent,
via the djhshih/blat fork. rblat is therefore governed by, and distributed under,
the ORIGINAL BLAT license reproduced verbatim below. rblat does not, and cannot,
relicense the bundled BLAT code, and the same terms extend to the rblat package
as a whole (see "rblat glue code" at the end).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ORIGINAL BLAT LICENSE (verbatim, from the djhshih/blat fork's LICENSE.txt; the
per-file copyright headers read "Copyright <years> Jim Kent.  All rights
reserved."):

    All files are copyrighted, but license is hereby granted for personal,
    academic, and non-profit use.  A license is also granted for the contents
    of the top level lib and inc directories for commercial users.  Commercial
    users should contact jim_kent@pacbell.net for access to other modules.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

What this means for rblat (IMPORTANT):

  * Personal, academic, and non-profit use of rblat is permitted under the
    grant above.

  * The commercial grant in the original license covers ONLY the top-level
    `lib` and `inc` directories. rblat links the BLAT ALIGNER CORE -- the
    "other modules" -- including blat.c (as src/rblat_blat.c), genoFind.c,
    fuzzyFind.c, supStitch.c, gfClientLib.c, gfBlatLib.c, and bandExt.c.
    These are NOT within the lib/inc commercial grant.

  * Therefore COMMERCIAL USE of rblat (including use at or on behalf of a
    for-profit entity) requires a separate license for those modules. Contact
    jim_kent@pacbell.net, or Kent Informatics (https://kentinformatics.com),
    for commercial licensing of BLAT / gfServer / gfClient and In-Silico PCR.

  * Because of the above, rblat CANNOT be redistributed under a permissive
    open-source license (MIT, GPL, etc.). It inherits the BLAT terms in full.

  This is directly relevant to for-profit affiliations: running rblat there requires a commercial BLAT
  license from Kent Informatics.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
rblat glue code
---------------

The rblat-specific glue authored for this package -- the R wrappers, the C
registration/entry points and engine adapter (src/rblat_*.c, src/rblat.h),
the build files, tests, and documentation -- is Copyright (c) 2026 Robert
Scharpf. As distributed with the bundled BLAT sources, the combined work is
governed by the BLAT license above.
